   "id": "e9595338ca",
   "es": "Tener que y no hace falta",
   "kinds": [
    "lesson.title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "729e46fc90",
   "es": "Hablar de obligaciones y de lo que no es necesario: have to, must, don't have to.",
   "kinds": [
    "lesson.objective"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "8026606a72",
   "es": "Have to y must expresan obligación: I have to wear a uniform. Don't have to NO es una prohibición: dice que algo no hace falta (You don't have to come). En pasado: had to (tuve que).",
   "kinds": [
    "lesson.intro"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "342750c0ab",
   "es": "Cuentas tus obligaciones con have to y must.",
   "kinds": [
    "lesson.takeaway"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "1eb13761a2",
   "es": "Dices que algo no hace falta con don't have to.",
   "kinds": [
    "lesson.takeaway"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "65cf5025bb",
   "es": "Have to + verbo: obligación. Must va sin to (I must wear).",
   "kinds": [
    "exercise.explanation"
   ],
   "en": "have"
  },
  {
   "id": "6b41e8b747",
   "es": "Es gratis. No hace falta pagar.",
